# Deliberately no SPA catch-all.
#
# react/public/_redirects carries `/*  /index.html  200`, which is correct for
# the React single-page app: it has one HTML entry point and routes on the
# client. The Astro build does not. Every route here is prerendered to its own
# file (build.format: 'file'), so a catch-all only has one effect — it swallows
# every unmatched path and answers with the homepage at HTTP 200. That makes
# 404.html unreachable and turns every dead link into a soft 404 that search
# engines index as a real page.
#
# With no rule matching, the host falls through to 404.html and returns a real
# 404. Clean URLs (/operators -> operators.html) are asset resolution, not a
# redirect rule, so they are unaffected.
#
# This file is listed in ASTRO_OWNED in astro/scripts/sync-public.mjs so the
# react copy is not mirrored back over it on the next build.
